H1400.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1399 (גְּבַר)
{a person}
KJV: certain, man.

H1401.definition:
(Aramaic) intensive of H1400 (גְּבַר);
valiant, or warrior
KJV: mighty.

H1402.definition:
intensive of H1399 (גְּבַר);
Gibbar, an Israelite
KJV: Gibbar.

H1403.definition:
from H1397 (גֶּבֶר) and H410 (אֵל); man of God;
Gabriel, an archangel
KJV: Garbriel.

H1404.definition:
feminine of H1376 (גְּבִיר);
mistress
KJV: lady, mistress.

H1405.definition:
intensive from H1389 (גִּבְעָה); a hilly spot;
Gibbethon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gibbethon.

H1406.definition:
probably by reduplication from H1342 (גָּאָה);
a roof; by analogy, the top of an altar
KJV: roof (of the house), (house) top (of the house).

H1407.definition:
from H1413 (גָּדַד) (in the sense of cutting);
coriander seed (from its furrows)
KJV: coriander.

H1408.definition:
a variation of H1409 (גָּד);
Fortune, a Babylonian deity
KJV: that troop.

H1409.definition:
from H1464 (גּוּד) (in the sense of distributing);
fortune
KJV: troop.

H1410.definition:
from H1464 (גּוּד);
Gad, a son of Jacob, including his tribe and its territory; also a prophet
KJV: Gad.

H1411.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1489 (גִּזְבָּר);
a treasurer
KJV: treasurer.

H1412.definition:
by reduplication from H1413 (גָּדַד) (in the sense of cutting) cleft;
Gudgodah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Gudgodah.

H1413.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1464 (גּוּד));
to crowd; also to gash (as if by pressing into)
KJV: assemble (selves by troops), gather (selves together, self in troops), cut selves.

H1414.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1413 (גָּדַד);
to cut down
KJV: hew down.

H1415.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to cut off);
a border of a river (as cut into by the stream)
KJV: bank.

H1416.definition:
from H1413 (גָּדַד);
a crowd (especially of soldiers)
KJV: army, band (of men), company, troop (of robbers).

H1417.definition:
or גְּדֻדָה; (feminine) from H1413 (גָּדַד);
a furrow (as cut)
KJV: furrow.

H1418.definition:
feminine participle passive of H1413 (גָּדַד);
an incision
KJV: cutting.

H1419.definition:
or גָּדֹל; (shortened) from H1431 (גָּדַל);
great (in any sense); hence, older; also insolent
KJV: [phrase] aloud, elder(-est), [phrase] exceeding(-ly), [phrase] far, (man of) great (man, matter, thing,-er,-ness), high, long, loud, mighty, more, much, noble, proud thing, [idiom] sore, ([idiom]) very.

H1420.definition:
or גְּדֻלָּה; (shortened) or (less accurately) גְּדוּלָּה; feminine of H1419 (גָּדוֹל);
greatness; (concretely) mighty acts
KJV: dignity, great things(-ness), majesty.

H1421.definition:
or (shortened) גִּדֻּף; and (feminine) גִּדּוּפָהxlit giddûphâh corrected to giddûwphâh; or גִּדֻּפָה; from H1422 (גְּדוּפָה);
vilification
KJV: reproach, reviling.

H1422.definition:
feminine passive participle of H1442 (גָּדַף);
a revilement
KJV: taunt.

H1423.definition:
from the same as H1415 (גָּדָה);
a young goat (from browsing)
KJV: kid.

H1424.definition:
from H1409 (גָּד); fortunate;
Gadi, an Israelite
KJV: Gadi.

H1425.definition:
patronymically from H1410 (גָּד);
a Gadite (collectively) or descendants of Gad
KJV: Gadites, children of Gad.

H1426.definition:
intensive for H1424 (גָּדִי);
Gaddi, an Israelite
KJV: Gaddi.

H1427.definition:
from H1409 (גָּד) and H410 (אֵל); fortune of God;
Gaddiel, an Israelite
KJV: Gaddiel.

H1428.definition:
or גַּדיָה; the same as H1415 (גָּדָה);
a river brink
KJV: bank.

H1429.definition:
feminine of H1423 (גְּדִי);
a young female goat
KJV: kid.

H1430.definition:
from an unused root (meaning to heap up);
a stack of sheaves; by analogy, a tomb
KJV: shock (stack) (of corn), tomb.

H1432.definition:
from H1431 (גָּדַל);
large (literally or figuratively)
KJV: great, grew.

H1433.definition:
from H1431 (גָּדַל);
magnitude (literally or figuratively)
KJV: greatness, stout(-ness).

H1434.definition:
from H1431 (גָּדַל) (in the sense of twisting);
thread, i.e. a tassel or festoon
KJV: fringe, wreath.

H1435.definition:
from H1431 (גָּדַל); stout;
Giddel, the name of one of the Nethinim, also of one of 'Solomon's servants'
KJV: Giddel.

H1436.definition:
or (prolonged) גְּדַלְיָהוּ; from H1431 (גָּדַל) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has become great;
Gedaljah, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Gedaliah.

H1437.definition:
from H1431 (גָּדַל); I have made great;
Giddalti, an Israelite
KJV: Giddalti.

H1438.definition:
a primitive root;
to fell a tree; generally, to destroy anything
KJV: cut (asunder, in sunder, down, off), hew down.

H1439.definition:
from H1438 (גָּדַע); feller (i.e. warrior);
Gidon, an Israelite
KJV: Gideon.

H1440.definition:
from H1438 (גָּדַע); a cutting (i.e. desolation);
Gidom, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gidom.

H1441.definition:
from H1438 (גָּדַע); warlike (compare H1439 (גִּדְעוֹן));
Gidoni, an Israelite
KJV: Gideoni.

H1442.definition:
a primitive root;
to hack (with words), i.e. revile
KJV: blaspheme, reproach.

H1443.definition:
a primitive root;
to wall in or around
KJV: close up, fence up, hedge, inclose, make up (a wall), mason, repairer.

H1444.definition:
from H1443 (גָּדַר);
a circumvallation
KJV: wall.

H1445.definition:
; the same as H1444 (גֶּדֶר);
Geder, a place in Palestine
KJV: Geder.

H1446.definition:
or (fully) גְּדוֹר; from H1443 (גָּדַר); inclosure;
Gedor, a place in Palestine; also the name of three Israelites
KJV: Gedor.

H1447.definition:
from H1443 (גָּדַר);
a circumvallation; by implication, an inclosure
KJV: fence, hedge, wall.

H1448.definition:
feminine of H1447 (גָּדֵר);
enclosure (especially for flocks)
KJV: (sheep-) cote (fold) hedge, wall.

H1449.definition:
the same as H1448 (גְּדֵרָה);
(with the article) Gederah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gederah, hedges.

H1450.definition:
plural of H1448 (גְּדֵרָה); walls;
Gederoth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gederoth.

H1451.definition:
patrial from H1445 (גֶּדֶר);
a Gederite, or inhabitant of Geder
KJV: Gederite.

H1452.definition:
patrial from H1449 (גְּדֵרָה);
a Gederathite, or inhabitant of Gederah
KJV: Gederathite.

H1453.definition:
dual of H1448 (גְּדֵרָה); double wall;
Gederothajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gederothaim.

H1454.definition:
probably a clerical error for H2088 (זֶה);
this
KJV: this.

H1455.definition:
a primitive root;
to remove (a bandage from a wound, i.e. heal it)
KJV: cure.

H1456.definition:
from H1455 (גָּהָה);
a cure
KJV: medicine.

H1457.definition:
a primitive root;
to prostrate oneself
KJV: cast self down, stretch self.

H1458.definition:
another form for H1460 (גֵּו);
the back
KJV: back.

H1459.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1460 (גֵּו);
the middle
KJV: midst, same, there-(where-) in.

H1460.definition:
from H1342 (גָּאָה) (corresponding to H1354 (גַב));
the back; by analogy, the middle
KJV: [phrase] among, back, body.

H1461.definition:
a primitive root;
to dig
KJV: husbandman.

H1462.definition:
from H1461 (גּוּב);
the locust (from its grubbing as a larvae)
KJV: grasshopper, [idiom] great.

H1463.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Gog, the name of an Israelite, also of some nothern nation
KJV: Gog.

H1464.definition:
a primitive root (akin to H1413 (גָּדַד));
to crowd upon, i.e. attack
KJV: invade, overcome.

H1465.definition:
feminine of H1460 (גֵּו);
the back, i.e. (by extensive) the person
KJV: body.

H1466.definition:
the same as H1465 (גֵּוָה);
exaltation; (figuratively) arrogance
KJV: lifting up, pride.

H1467.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1466 (גֵּוָה)
{exaltation; (figuratively) arrogance}
KJV: pride.

H1468.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1494 (גַּזָז));
properly, to shear off; but used only in the (figuratively) sense of passing rapidly
KJV: bring, cut off.

H1469.definition:
or (shortened) גֹזָלlemma גזָל missing vowel, corrected to גֹזָל; from H1497 (גָּזַל);
a nestling (as being comparatively nude of feathers)
KJV: young (pigeon).

H1470.definition:
probably from H1468 (גּוּז); a quarry (as a place of cutting stones);
Gozan, a province of Assyria
KJV: Gozan.

H1471.definition:
rarely (shortened) גֹּי; apparently from the same root as H1465 (גֵּוָה) (in the sense of massing);
a foreign nation; hence, a Gentile; also (figuratively) a troop of animals, or a flight of locusts
KJV: Gentile, heathen, nation, people.

H1472.definition:
prolonged for H1465 (גֵּוָה);
a body, whether alive or dead
KJV: (dead) body, carcase, corpse.

H1473.definition:
or (shortened) גֹּלָה; active participle feminine of H1540 (גָּלָה);
exile; concretely and collectively exiles
KJV: (carried away), captive(-ity), removing.

H1474.definition:
from H1473 (גּוֹלָה); captive;
Golan, a place east of the Jordan
KJV: Golan.

H1475.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a pit
KJV: pit.

H1476.definition:
probably from H1598 (גָּנַן); protected;
Guni, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Guni.

H1477.definition:
patronymically from H1476 (גּוּנִי);
a Gunite (collectively with article prefix) or descendants of Guni
KJV: Gunites.

H1478.definition:
a primitive root;
to breathe out, i.e. (by implication) expire
KJV: die, be dead, give up the ghost, perish.

H1479.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to hollow or arch, i.e. (figuratively) close; to shut
KJV: shut.

H1480.definition:
from H1479 (גּוּף);
a corpse (as closed to sense)
KJV: body.

H1481.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to turn aside from the road (for a lodging or any other purpose), i.e. sojourn (as a guest); also to shrink, fear (as in a strange place); also to gather forhostility (as afraid)
KJV: abide, assemble, be afraid, dwell, fear, gather (together), inhabitant, remain, sojourn, stand in awe, (be) stranger, [idiom] surely.

H1482.definition:
or (shortened) גֻּר; perhaps from H1481 (גּוּר);
a cub (as still abiding in the lair), especially of the lion
KJV: whelp, young one.

H1483.definition:
the same as H1482 (גּוּר);
Gur, a place in Palestine
KJV: Gur.

H1484.definition:
or (feminine) גֹּרָה; a variation of H1482 (גּוּר)
{a cub (as still abiding in the lair), especially of the lion}
KJV: whelp.

H1485.definition:
from H1481 (גּוּר) and H1168 (בַּעַל); dwelling of Baal;
Gur-Baal, a place in Arabia
KJV: Gur-baal.

H1486.definition:
or (shortened) גֹּרָל; from an unused root meaning to be rough (as stone);
properly, a pebble, i.e. a lot (small stones being used for that purpose); figuratively, a portion or destiny (as if determined by lot)
KJV: lot.

H1487.definition:
or rather (by permutation) גִּישׁ; of uncertain derivation;
a mass of earth
KJV: clod.

H1488.definition:
from H1494 (גַּזָז);
a fleece (as shorn); also mown grass
KJV: fleece, mowing, mown grass.

H1489.definition:
of foreign derivation;
treasurer
KJV: treasurer.

H1491.definition:
a primitive root (akin to H1468 (גּוּז));
to cut off, i.e. portion out
KJV: take.

H1492.definition:
feminine from H1494 (גַּזָז);
a fleece
KJV: fleece.

H1493.definition:
patrial from the unused name of a place apparently in Palestine;
a Gizonite or inhabitant of Gizoh
KJV: Gizonite.

H1494.definition:
a primitive root (akin to H1468 (גּוּז));
to cut off; specifically to shear aflock or shave the hair; figuratively to destroy an enemy
KJV: cut off (down), poll, shave, (sheep-) shear(-er).

H1495.definition:
from H1494 (גַּזָז); shearer;
Gazez, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Gazez.

H1496.definition:
from H1491 (גָּזָה);
something cut, i.e. dressed stone
KJV: hewed, hewn stone, wrought.

H1497.definition:
a primitive root;
to pluck off; specifically to flay, strip or rob
KJV: catch, consume, exercise (robbery), pluck (off), rob, spoil, take away (by force, violence), tear.

H1498.definition:
from H1497 (גָּזַל);
robbery, or (concretely) plunder
KJV: robbery, thing taken away by violence.

H1499.definition:
from H1497 (גָּזַל);
plunder, i.e. violence
KJV: violence, violent perverting.. gozal. See H1469 (גּוֹזָל).
